1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
Follow account creation, security key registration, and login.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:07,400
Watch the typed entries and illustrated security prompts.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,854
Start with Create database user.

4
00:00:09,854 --> 00:00:13,563
The administrator enters the demo administrator token and root
password.

5
00:00:13,563 --> 00:00:20,238
Then choose a new username, and type the password that this user
will use for registration and login.

6
00:00:20,238 --> 00:00:21,721
Passwords appear as dots.

7
00:00:21,721 --> 00:00:25,801
Leave the drop account option unchecked, and click Create MySQL
user.

8
00:00:25,801 --> 00:00:29,880
The confirmation tells you to register the user's security key next.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,068
Move to registration.

10
00:00:36,068 --> 00:00:39,629
Type the username and password for the account just created.

11
00:00:39,629 --> 00:00:43,190
Click Register in browser to open the security key prompt.

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,862
Choose the connected security key.

13
00:00:48,862 --> 00:00:52,960
The browser or operating system asks for the key's security PIN.

14
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:56,312
Enter that PIN in the security prompt, then continue.

15
00:00:56,312 --> 00:00:59,292
Next, touch the security key when it flashes.

16
00:00:59,292 --> 00:01:04,135
The PIN belongs to the key; it is different from the database
password.

17
00:01:04,135 --> 00:01:06,370
These illustrated prompts show the sequence.

18
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:09,350
The registration confirmation appears back in the application.

19
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,959
To log in, enter the same username and database password.

20
00:01:15,959 --> 00:01:17,542
Click Authenticate to MySQL.

21
00:01:17,542 --> 00:01:23,480
The browser now requests the registered security key, which is the
user's physical security token.

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,571
Use the registered key and touch its flashing contact.

23
00:01:28,571 --> 00:01:33,332
Login uses your database password and security token, without
entering a PIN.

24
00:01:33,332 --> 00:01:36,110
The key signs the authentication challenge automatically.

25
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:38,362
Success.

26
00:01:38,362 --> 00:01:41,977
Hello world appears with the authenticated account and connection
details.

27
00:01:41,977 --> 00:01:47,400
The application screens are real; the database and security device
are simulated for this walkthrough.
